  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1217 PM CDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nThe long term forecast looks a little bleak with hot temperatures \nand no precipitation chances in sight. The upper ridging is expected \nto continue expanding east across the Gulf states over the weekend. \nModels indicate the upper ridging will remain parked over the \nsoutheastern CONUS through much of next week. Subsidence below the \nridging will keep precipitation chances near zero. At the moment, \ntemperatures are not forecasted to be as hot as this past week with \nhighs only in the upper 90s to lower 100s. However, during this \ntime, the NBM underestimated high temperatures. If this continues, \ncould see possible Heat Advisory temperatures (105-109 degrees), \nespecially off the Caprock.",
